{"name":"Gramp’s Tea Cup","hex":"#e9dec8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gramp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Grandpa, grandfather."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gramp"},{"term":"tea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Temiar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tea plant (Camellia sinensis);  a variety of this plant.","The dried leaves or buds of the tea plant;  a variety of such leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea"},{"term":"cup","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Cupeño."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concave vessel for drinking, usually made of opaque material (as opposed to a glass) and with a handle.","The contents of said vessel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cup"}],"entries":[{"title":"Teacup","blocks":[{"text":"A teacup is a cup for drinking tea. It generally has a small handle that may be grasped with the thumb and one or two fingers. It is typically made of a ceramic material and is often part of a set which is composed of a cup and a matching saucer or a trio that includes a small cake or sandwich plate. These may be part of a tea set combined with a teapot, cream jug, covered sugar bowl, and slop bowl. Teacups are often wider and shorter than coffee cups. Cups for morning tea are conventionally larger than cups for afternoon tea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Five_Piece_Tea_Service_with_Chrysanthemum_Design_LACMA_M.2006.132.10a-i.jpg/330px-Five_Piece_Tea_Service_with_Chrysanthemum_Design_LACMA_M.2006.132.10a-i.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teacup","wikidata":"Q81707"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"},{"title":"Cup","blocks":[{"text":"A cup is a small container used to hold liquids for drinking, typically with a flattened hemispherical shape and an open \"mouth\", and often with a capacity of about 6–16 US fluid ounces (177–473 ml). Cups may be made of pottery, glass, metal, wood, stone, polystyrene, plastic, lacquerware, or other materials. Normally, a cup is brought in contact with the mouth for drinking, distinguishing it from other tableware and drinkware forms such as jugs; however, a straw and/or lid may also be used. They also often have handles, though many do not, including beakers which have no handle or stem, or small bowl shapes which are very common in Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cup_and_Saucer_LACMA_47.35.6a-b_%281_of_3%29.jpg/330px-Cup_and_Saucer_LACMA_47.35.6a-b_%281_of_3%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cup","wikidata":"Q81727"},{"title":"Grandparent","blocks":[{"text":"Grandparents, individually known as grandmother and grandfather, or Grandma and Grandpa, are the parents of a person's father or mother – paternal or maternal. Every sexually reproducing living organism who is not a genetic chimera has a maximum of 4 genetic grandparents, 8 genetic great-grandparents, 16 genetic great-great-grandparents, 32 genetic great-great-great-grandparents, 64 genetic great-great-great-great-grandparents, etc. In the history of modern humanity, around 30,000 years ago, the number of modern humans who lived to be a grandparent increased. It is not known for certain what spurred this increase in longevity, but it is generally believed that a key consequence of three generations being alive together was the preservation of information which could otherwise have been lost; an example of this important information might have been where to find water in times of drought."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/The_Favorite_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg/330px-The_Favorite_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grandparent","wikidata":"Q167918"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Small_black_and_green_CUP_no_handle.JPG/500px-Small_black_and_green_CUP_no_handle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Small_black_and_green_CUP_no_handle.JPG/1280px-Small_black_and_green_CUP_no_handle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Small_black_and_green_CUP_no_handle.JPG/500px-Small_black_and_green_CUP_no_handle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tea bowl without a handle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmall_black_and_green_CUP_no_handle.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Camellia_sinensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-025.jpg/500px-Camellia_sinensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Camellia_sinensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-025.jpg/1280px-Camellia_sinensis_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-025.jpg?utm_source